    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against questionable starters, with **Corbin Carroll** (81.55) and **James Wood** (76.28) headlining our offensive attack. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a prime #3 spot and a favorable matchup against Andre Pallante; his elite sprint speed is further magnified by a 100% stolen base opportunity rating against this battery, locking him in as an anchor. Similarly, **James Wood** thrives against Jacob Lopez, utilizing his elite 0.433 xwOBA and a +19% boost from a favorable pitcher skill matchup to reach the highest projection on the board. We are also leaning heavily into **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) as a high-value play against Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez, though we must monitor the 45% rain risk in that stadium to ensure he stays in the lineup.\n\nOur optimization strategy continues to prioritize the scarcity of stolen bases, which keeps players like **Brice Turang** (60.25) in the starting nine despite a tough draw against Eury P\u00e9rez. **Brice Turang** is buoyed by a +4% boost stemming from the opposing battery's slow delivery, creating a rare window for larceny. On the bench, **Zach McKinstry** (52.89) was the most difficult exclusion; he offered a strong +19% matchup bump against Ryan Johnson, but his lower base projection and the inherent volatility of a #7 lineup spot left him just shy of the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are also keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency sits at a basement-level 46.89; if his spot remains deep in the order, he remains a candidate to be swapped for a bench asset with a higher probability of contributing to our AVG or R categories.",
